# FastAPI Instagram-Style Backend Service

A modular backend CRUD API built with **FastAPI** and **PostgreSQL**, structured according to production best practices with versioned routing and segregated schemas.

---
## System Flowchart & Architecture

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    Client["Incoming HTTP Request"] --> Main["main.py<br/>(Boots App & Mounts /api/v1 Router)"]
    Main --> Router["api/v1/posts/router.py<br/>(Route Handler: GET, POST, PUT, DELETE)"]
    
    Router -->|Validates Payload| Schemas["schemas.py<br/>(Pydantic V2 Schemas)<br/>- PostCreate (Input)<br/>- PostResponse (Output)"]
    Router -->|Fetches / Saves Data| Models["models.py<br/>(SQLAlchemy ORM Model)<br/>Table: posts"]
    
    Models --> DB["database.py<br/>(Engine, SessionLocal, get_db)"]
    DB --> Postgres[("PostgreSQL Database")]




## Project Architecture

```text
app/
├── api/
│   └── v1/
│       └── posts/
│           ├── __init__.py
│           ├── router.py       # Posts endpoints (/api/v1/posts)
│           └── schemas.py      # Pydantic models for validation
│
├── db/
│   ├── __init__.py
│   └── database.py             # PostgreSQL connection & cursor handling
│
├── main.py                     # Minimal application entrypoint
├── requirements.txt
└── README.md


uvicorn main: app --reload
